p: .
t. 
|  
|  Family court judges have many ways of attacking protective mothers
|  who appear before them as litigants. Since many of these attacks make
|  little sense either logically or legally, one tends to look elsewhere for an
|  explanation. A likely underlying reason is that the protective mother
|  (or her attorney, sympathetic caseworkers or therapists, or others who
.  support her position) presents a perceived threat to the judge’s authority


--- Sentence/switch
id: 2
r#  457  12  76

--- Paragraph/end 
id: 1
