|  A particularly dramatic example occurred in a California case that
|  unfolded in the late 1990s (and is still not fully resolved). In
|  1995, the mother had sole physical (and
|  joint legal) custody of her three school-age children, two of whom (two
|  girls, ages four and six) had complained of being sexually abused during
|  visitation with their father. A medical examination carried out at the
|  University of California, Davis, Medical Center showed that the older
|  girl had thickened folds of the anus, generalized increased vascularity of the perihymenal tissue, and an irregular, narrow thickened
|  hymenal wall.\79The judge assigned a law guardian and a court-appointed evaluator
|  to interview the mother and her children. However, the law guardian
